

- `action(n1, "start buyer process")`: Hallucinates an undocumented step; the source explicitly states "the process begins by choosing a book" with no preceding initialization action.
- `actor(a_default, "Default", [i1, n1, n2, ...])`: Violates actor fidelity; the source assigns all process responsibilities to "buyers", not a generic "Default" participant.
- `label(n5, c1, "After selecting preferred copy")` and `label(n8, c1, "After selecting preferred copy")`: Misaligns with source semantics; the text only associates copy selection with the details or used-copies paths ("proceed to select a copy and end the process" / "select their preferred copy"), not with the paths that merely "view list of new copies".
- `defines(v1, "choose what to do after selecting book", {})` and `defines(v2, "choose what to do after viewing book details", {})`: Value ranges are empty `{}`, failing to faithfully capture the explicit choice options enumerated in the source ("view the book details or see a list of new copies... view a list of used copies").